<p><strong>Administrator role and permissions</strong></p>
<p class="subclause">1. Administrator is as the Merchant&rsquo;s prime contact person with Nuvei</p>
<p class="subclause">2. It is recommended that the Administrator will be a senior position holder with the Merchant.</p>
<p class="subclause">3. The Administrator is granted full access/action permission to the Merchant&rsquo;s account(s) on Nuvei&rsquo;s Control Panel with the exception of the APM Pricing Management Section (as defined below).</p>
<p class="subclause">4. The Administrator may appoint additional authorized users to the Nuvei Control Panel and set/change permission to such authorized users. Such permission explicitly excludes appointment of or setting/changing permission to the APM Pricing Manager Section. Unless specifically requested by the Merchant or by the Administrator, the Administrator is the only person authorized on behalf of the Merchant to define, allocate, and manage the access of the Merchant&rsquo;s additional Authorized Users to the Nuvei Control Panel. This includes, but is not limited to, role management, requesting password re-allocation, granting a shared login, etc. (jointly: &ldquo;Administrator Permissions&rdquo;).</p>
<p class="subclause">5. The Merchant specifically authorizes the Administrator to appoint Authorized Users with Administrator Permissions, same as the initial Administrator without the need for Merchant approval. Merchant is fully aware of the scope and potential consequences of such permission.</p>
<p class="subclause">6. When approaching Nuvei, the Administrator and authorized users will be taken through security procedures to identify the caller.</p>

