<p style="margin-top:14pt;"><strong>APM Pricing Manager role and permissions:</strong></p>
<p class="subclause">1. &ldquo;Alternative Payment Method&rdquo; or &ldquo;APM&rdquo; means a payment method (other than Cards) which Nuvei is able and has agreed to process (as notified by Nuvei to the Merchant from time to time)</p>
<p class="subclause">2. APM Pricing Manager is appointed by the Merchant as its designated person and authorized signatory for the management of APMs using the Nuvei Control Panel. The APM Pricing Manager is authorized to: (i) confirm/decline processing selected APMs under their specified pricing and terms, and (ii) confirm/decline change to a selected APM&rsquo;s specified pricing (applicable for a previously approved APM).</p>
<p class="subclause">For the avoidance of doubt, in addition to merchant confirmation of an APM and its specified pricing and terms, processing of said APM is also subject to further configuration and activation by Nuvei.</p>
<p class="subclause">3. It is Mandatory that the APM Pricing Manager will be the Merchant&rsquo;s authorized signatory or be appointed by the Merchant&rsquo;s authorized signatory.</p>
<p class="subclause">4. The APM Pricing Manager is granted full access/action permission to the Merchant&rsquo;s APM pricing management section on the Merchant&rsquo;s Nuvei&rsquo;s Control Panel account (the &ldquo;APM Pricing Management Section&rdquo;).</p>
<p class="subclause">5. The APM Pricing Management Section is in addition to and does not derogate from the &lsquo;Alternative Payments Methods.&rsquo; section in the Agreements (the &ldquo;Agreements APM section&rdquo;). In case of any discrepancy between the terms of the Agreements and those of the APM Pricing Management Section the terms last agreed in writing prevails.</p>
<p class="subclause">6. The APM Pricing Manager MAY NOT appoint additional Authorized Users or APM Pricing Manager roles. the APM Pricing Manager is the only person authorized on behalf of the Merchant to access the APM Pricing Management Section.</p>
<p class="subclause">7. Merchant acknowledges that, notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Agreement, actions taken by the APM Pricing Manager on the Nuvei Control Panel shall be considered as the Merchant&rsquo;s legal, valid, and binding obligation, enforceable against it. Such actions shall be considered as if executed in writing, as legally binding to the Merchant, and as amending the terms of the Agreement (where applicable), without requiring the written signature of Nuvei. Merchant is fully aware of the scope and potential consequences of such actions.</p>
<p class="subclause">8. When approaching Nuvei, the APM Pricing Manager will be taken through security procedures to identify the caller.</p>

<h3>Nuvei Control Panel Terms of Use</h3>
<h4>A. Authorized Users</h4>
<p class="subclause">1. Account Activation email shall be initiated by the Nuvei Control Panel directly to the email address of the APM Pricing Manager, Administrator and those users authorized by the Administrator. The Administrator and such authorized users, specifically excluding APM Pricing Manager role, shall be referred to jointly as &ldquo;Authorized User&rdquo;.</p>
<p class="subclause">2. Unless expressly waived by Nuvei, only company email domain addresses are acceptable for Authorized Users and APM Pricing Manager (i.e. not Hotmail, Gmail, Yahoo, etc.).</p>
<p class="subclause">3. Generic email accounts (e.g. admin@companyname.xxx) must be a role-based email account used only by the Administrator or APM Pricing Manager and may not be internal.</p>
<p class="subclause">4. Change in Administrator/ APM Pricing Manager/password reset: Changing Administrator or APM Pricing Manager details and password resets are available by calling the Nuvei Technical Support Team. A password reset may only be initiated by the Administrator or APM Pricing Manager, and only for their respective roles. The Administrator is authorized to perform all of the above for the Authorized Users.</p>
<p class="subclause">5. Changes in Administrator and/or APM Pricing Manager (unless more than one Administrator and/or APM Pricing Manager exists) would require re-submitting this form.</p>
<p class="subclause">6. The Merchant shall not attempt, nor permit persons who are not identified in this document, or by the Administrator, and confirmed by Nuvei as Authorized Users or as APM Pricing Manager(s), to access the Nuvei Control Panel.</p>
<p class="subclause">7. Nuvei treats any action taken whilst an Authorized User or APM Pricing Manager was logged into the Nuvei Control Panel as having been authorized by the Merchant. Nuvei shall not be responsible for any loss occurring as a result of a failure to maintain access permissions or to keep them sufficiently secure.</p>
<p class="subclause">8. The Merchant is responsible to ensure that all Authorized Users and APM Pricing Manager(s) comply with the terms of this document and any other reasonable instructions or recommendations Nuvei may issue.</p>
<p class="subclause">9. The Merchant is responsible to terminate permissions for Administrators, APM Pricing Manager or Authorized Users that have left the company.</p>

<h4>B. General</h4>
<p class="subclause">1. The Merchant represents and warrants that it has in place, and shall continue to maintain and enforce, stringent security policies that address, among others, the proper guidelines for Authorized Users and APM Pricing Manager(s) to the use of the Nuvei Control Panel, as well as how to retain and safeguard user IDs and passwords, such as periodical password changes, prohibition of usage of public computers/networks, and disablement of utilities/browsers that remember username/password, etc.</p>
<p class="subclause">2. Any person who enters the correct account identification and security validation and verification information on the Nuvei Control Panel will be able to access the Merchant&rsquo;s account allowing Nuvei to treat any transaction conducted by that person as valid and authorized by Merchant. Nuvei will not be held responsible for any loss or damage the Merchant may incur as a result.</p>
<p class="subclause">3. Breach or suspected breach &ndash; It is the Merchant&rsquo;s responsibility to notify Nuvei immediately (phone: +44-2030513031; email: enterprise.support@nuvei.com) when the Merchant Knows/suspects that an allocated User ID and/or password have been compromised or are the risk of being compromised. The Merchant is further responsible that the Authorized Users and/or APM Pricing Manager(s) immediately change passwords in the event of such breach or suspected breach.</p>
<p class="subclause">4. The Merchant fully agrees to use the Nuvei Control Panel at the Merchant&rsquo;s sole risk. The Nuvei Control Panel is accessed through the Internet, which is a public system over which Nuvei has no control.</p>
<p class="subclause">5. The service is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &rdquo;as available&rdquo; basis without any warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, statutory, or otherwise, and Nuvei will not be responsible if the service does not work properly. Nuvei does not warrant or make any representations regarding the use, or the results of the use, of the Nuvei Control Panel in terms of availability, correctness, accuracy, timelines, completeness, reliability, or otherwise and disclaims on behalf of itself and its affiliates and their respective directors, shareholders, employees and otherwise any liability or responsibility from any use or interpretation of, or reliance upon, the Nuvei Control Panel.</p>
<p class="subclause">6. Nuvei reserves the right to change the terms of this service and the access guidelines and requirements to the Nuvei Control Panel at any time and without notice. Nuvei may at any time suspend or otherwise restrict certain or all functionalities and/or access permissions including where Nuvei suspects unauthorized access or use or compromise of the account security.</p>
<p class="subclause">7. Any loss sustained by the Merchant due to non-compliance with these guidelines will be at the Merchant&rsquo;s own risk and responsibility, and Nuvei will not be liable for the same in any manner.</p>
<p class="subclause">8. These terms of use and the use of Nuvei Control Panel are at all times subject to and governed by the Agreement, as such, Agreement provisions are adopted herein by reference and the availability of the Nuvei Control Panel is subject to the Agreement remaining in effect.</p>

